{"agent_id":"pp3g-bJpy-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-0c0e","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:01:20.846687639Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"1cd0b4e4-d6e6-470b-8ae5-96e2e302f8f3","author":"pp3g-bJpy-read-only-plan-review-do-not-modify-files-do-not-0c0e","content":"[RESULT] INDEPENDENT ADVERSARIAL REVIEW — P3 'Safe re-hydration guard' plan (2026-08-06). Scope: independent verification of plan + big-pickle verdict against crosslink source. No files modified. No commit. #125 NOT closed.\n\n== VERIFICATION TABLE ==\n\n| # | Claim | Source | Verdict | File:Line | Note |\n|---|-------|--------|---------|-----------|------|\n| 1 | maybe_auto_hydrate runs on EVERY command via get_db, NO HubMode gate | Plan + big-pickle | CONFIRM | main.rs:2292, hydration.rs:1184-1219 | get_db() calls maybe_auto_hydrate unconditionally; function has zero HubMode checks; goes straight to hydrate_to_sqlite(cache_dir, db) at line 1214 |\n| 2 | hydrate_to_sqlite preserves only created_by IS NULL rows | Plan + big-pickle | CONFIRM (nuanced) | hydration.rs:166-177 | The sqlite_only_rows filter (line 176: row.created_by.is_none()) is the PRESERVATION filter — it keeps only direct-SQLite rows. Agent-authored rows (created_by set) NOT in JSON are dropped. #119 (186b12ea) fixed hydrate_from_state (v3 path, line 350-366) to preserve ALL sqlite-only rows regardless of created_by; hydrate_to_sqlite (v2 path) was NOT fixed. This is the exact asymmetry that makes the auto-hydrate path lethal. |\n| 3 | init_cache v2-first: picks v2 branch when present, early-returns if cache exists | Plan + big-pickle | CONFIRM | sync/cache.rs:170-184 | Line 170-172: early return if cache_dir exists. Line 174-184: if v2 branch exists (remote or local), init_v2_worktree. The plan's 'v2-first contradiction' framing is partially valid but the fix is misdiagnosed (see finding below). |\n| 4 | HubMode::resolve degrades to V2 on detection error | Big-pickle | CONFIRM | hub_v3.rs:709-720 | Line 713-718: Err(e) => HubMode::V2 with debug log 'defaulting to V2'. A gate of hub_mode().is_v3() would silently re-enable v2 path under transient git failure. |\n| 5 | Trust commits land on checked-out v2 branch | Plan + big-pickle | CONFIRM | sync/trust.rs:385-412, 588-621 | publish_key (line 391-403): git add trust/ + commit in cache_dir (the v2 worktree). commit_allowed_signers_unsigned (line 588-621): same pattern. These advance the v2 branch tip. |\n| 6 | Agent bootstrap commits + pushes to HUB_BRANCH (v2) | Big-pickle finding 4 | CONFIRM | commands/agent.rs:668-690 | Line 668: git add agents/{id}/. Line 669-673: commit 'bootstrap: register agent'. Line 678: push HUB_BRANCH. Runs on EVERY kickoff launch. |\n| 7 | Swarm archive/reset commits + pushes to HUB_BRANCH | Big-pickle finding 4 | CONFIRM | commands/swarm/lifecycle.rs:128,200 | Line 128: push HUB_BRANCH (archive). Line 200: push HUB_BRANCH (reset). Also commit_hub_files at lines 312,465,768,887,1043. |\n| 8 | hydrate_from_state gated by is_v3 in shared_writer and locks_cmd | Plan reading (a) | CONFIRM | shared_writer/core.rs:204-218, locks_cmd.rs:246-265 | shared_writer: is_v3() check at line 204 routes to hydrate_from_state. locks_cmd sync_cmd: is_v3() check at line 246 routes to v3 hydration. These are the existing mode-gated v3 hydration paths. |\n| 9 | read_all_issue_files returns empty vec for missing dir | Big-pickle finding 7 | CONFIRM | issue_file.rs:225-229 | Line 228-229: if !issues_dir.exists() { return Ok(Vec::new()) }. Supports surgical mitigation soundness. |\n| 10 | #119 fix scope: hydrate_from_state ONLY, not hydrate_to_sqlite | Big-pickle | CONFIRM | hydration.rs:350-366 vs 166-177 | hydrate_from_state (v3) line 353-366: preserves all sqlite-only rows (created_by any value). hydrate_to_sqlite (v2) line 176: row.created_by.is_none() — only NULL. Asymmetric fix. |\n| 11 | ASES META_REF contains only hub.json, no allowed_signers | Big-pickle finding 5 | CONFIRM (live) | hub_v3.rs:580-606 (read path) | v3 reads allowed_signers from META_REF root tree (hub_source.rs). ASES META_REF = hub.json only. Trust writes to v2 branch are dead writes for v3 verification. |\n\n== PLAN PART (1) ASSESSMENT: GATE maybe_auto_hydrate ==\n\nThe plan's core fix (gate the v2 file path) is CORRECT. The defect is real and verified. Two refinements needed:\n\n(a) FAIL-CLOSED GATE: The plan says 'gate on hub mode (v3-only)'. Big-pickle correctly identifies that HubMode::resolve degrades to V2 on error (hub_v3.rs:713-718). A hub_mode().is_v3() gate would silently re-enable the destructive v2 path under transient git failure — precisely the concurrent-launch race (catalog 2.2). CONFIRM: gate on v3-REF PRESENCE directly (checkpoint/meta refs exist => skip), not on HubMode. This is fail-closed: if ref detection fails, the v2 path is skipped (conservative), not enabled (dangerous).\n\n(b) AMBIGUITY: 'hydrate only via hydrate_from_state from v3 refs' has two readings. Reading (a) = maybe_auto_hydrates no-ops on v3, hydration via existing mode-gated paths (shared_writer/core.rs:204, locks_cmd.rs:246). CONFIRM: these paths exist and work. This is cheap (no per-command cost). Reading (b) = implement v3 reduce+hydrate inside maybe_auto_hydrate. REJECT: would defeat the sub-millisecond design (main.rs:2286-2288) since compaction::reduce reads ALL agent refs. Plan MUST specify reading (a) explicitly.\n\n== PLAN PART (2) ASSESSMENT: FIX init_cache v2-first ==\n\nBig-pickle's finding 1 is CONFIRMED. The fix is misdiagnosed for three reasons:\n\n1. INERT for ASES: cache already exists (line 170-172 early return). Code change never re-hosts unless re-host logic is added — plan doesn't mention it.\n2. HARMFUL for hybrid repos: remigrate-from-v2 reads worktree issues/ files (migrate_hub_v3.rs:746-748, used at 1479). Re-hosting the worktree on v3 host branch hides v2 files from migration.\n3. DOES NOT remove wipe source: crosslink/hub-v3-host carries the SAME 4 stale June files (verified via live ASES state). The stale projection follows the re-host.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: Drop (2) from this plan. The v2-first precedence is deliberate migration support (cache.rs:150-157 doc). The defect is that the migration host doubles as ungated auto-hydrate source (fix 1) + write target (fix 3), not the precedence itself.\n\n== PLAN PART (3) ASSESSMENT: STOP trust commits on v2 branch ==\n\nBig-pickle's finding 4 is CONFIRMED. Part (3) covers only ONE of THREE v2-branch writers:\n- sync/trust.rs (plan covers this)\n- commands/agent.rs:668-690 (agent bootstrap — EVERY kickoff launch)\n- commands/swarm/lifecycle.rs:128,200 (swarm archive/reset)\n\nEven with fix (3), every kickoff launch still moves the v2 tip. This is HARMLESS only because fix (1) removes the wipe — but the plan should either widen (3) to all three writers or explicitly accept residual churn as out of scope.\n\nAlso confirm finding 5: trust writes to v2 are dead writes for v3 verification (v3 reads from META_REF, which has no allowed_signers in ASES). Stopping them costs nothing today. But there is no runtime path that updates META_REF allowed_signers either — if v3 trust is intended, that is new code and out of scope.\n\n== SURGICAL MITIGATION ASSESSMENT ==\n\nCONFIRM sound. The mitigation (rm -rf .crosslink/.hub-cache/issues) works because:\n- read_all_issue_files returns empty for missing dir (issue_file.rs:228-229)\n- hydrate_to_sqlite early-returns on empty (hydration.rs:126-128)\n- fetch_v2_readonly reset --hard is gated off when v3 (cache.rs:305-311)\n\nDocument on #125:\n- Restore command: git -C .crosslink/.hub-cache checkout -- issues\n- Footgun: restore BEFORE migrate hub-v3 --remigrate-from-v2 (reads those files, migrate_hub_v3.rs:746-748)\n- Future v2-mode downgrade re-arms the wipe\n- 4 negative-id rows (-1..-4) already persist in DB; acceptance criterion covers only NEW collisions\n\n== VERIFICATION ADEQUACY ==\n\nCONFIRM finding 6: no existing test for maybe_auto_hydrate. grep confirms only hydrate_to_sqlite/hydrate_from_state unit tests. cargo test passing does not verify the gate. Required regressions:\n(a) v3 hub + stale v2 files -> auto-hydrate must NOT wipe\n(b) V2Only hub STILL auto-hydrates (gate must not break legitimate v2)\n(c) Fail-closed: mode-detection error -> skip\n\n== SCOPE DELIMITATION ==\n\nCONFIRM finding 8: #125 is the whole family. State what this plan does NOT fix:\n- Catalog 2.3: worktree comment visibility\n- Catalog 2.4: uuid-sync quirk\n- Catalog 2.2 residual: concurrent explicit syncs both run hydrate_from_state\n\n== THINGS BOTH REVIEWS MISSED ==\n\n1. SYNC COMMAND ORDERING: get_db() is called BEFORE sync_cmd runs fetch. So maybe_auto_hydrate fires BEFORE fetch updates the v2 worktree. The wipe happens with STALE files, then sync's own hydration recovers. This ordering is the mechanism by which the wipe is both triggered and immediately recoverable — worth documenting.\n\n2. fetch_v2_readonly (cache.rs:328-357) resets --hard to remote tip. This would restore the v2 files after a surgical rm. So the mitigation is TEMPORARY — the next sync restores the stale files. But since fix (1) removes the auto-hydrate trigger, the restored files are inert (no one reads them for hydration).\n\n3. The empty-issue early return (hydration.rs:126-128) is a DATA-LOSS GUARD that already exists but is bypassed when the issues/ dir has files (the 4 June-era files). The fix removes the trigger, not the guard.\n\n== OVERALL VERDICT ==\n\nCHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nThe plan's mechanism analysis is verified correct. The core fix (1) is essential and correct but needs: (a) fail-closed gate on v3-ref presence (not HubMode), (b) explicit reading-(a) semantics (skip on v3; v3 hydration stays on existing paths). Part (2) should be dropped or re-scoped. Part (3) should be widened to all v2-branch writers or documented as accepting residual churn. Verification needs gate regression tests. Surgical mitigation is sound but needs documentation of restore command, remigrate footgun, and v2-downgrade re-arm.\n\nFix order: (1) fail-closed gate -> surgical rm -> (3) widen v2-branch writers. (2) should not gate the others. #125 left open.","created_at":"2026-08-06T07:01:20.814047031Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:TVyG47hpAGRXrbawVvEI00bKLyfpqIreUAeTPplyUyU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0maUcFizcWoS8kQ+XjtQ/Ml8ZxELFmgG/zob2uNpQKEAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJQtOyjo/h3OKo7HfiPFOgt4LGiA19oY9lf65pJDPKdauyk/nTX8g6Sztj2drluaqwEkp/ShD6VfWrbsLPzi3Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:TVyG47hpAGRXrbawVvEI00bKLyfpqIreUAeTPplyUyU","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg0maUcFizcWoS8kQ+XjtQ/Ml8ZxELFmgG/zob2uNpQKEAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNk7GfzktTNRu4VXfgav2EFrI5rPdllGby+zgNvKehY538jC21NWzB7IHBf9P20JC+Ot2gNbbtUXpZf1jfSDTgY="}
